# Maintainers' credentials for this repository, for jobs run from a maintainer's own machine.
#
# Copy to `.env.release` at the repository root and fill in what you need; it is gitignored. hq, the site and the other
# apps never read this file: their settings are in each app's own `.env.server` and `compose.env`. A contributor needs
# none of it.
#
# The keeper of every value is the team's vault: `scripts/secrets/export-to-vault.sh` after any change,
# `scripts/secrets/import-from-vault.sh` on a new machine (`.env.vault` says where the vault is).
# Read a value by name from a script (`set -a; . ./.env.release; set +a`) rather than opening the file, so no value is shown.

# --- Container registry ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider: GitHub (GitHub Container Registry, ghcr.io).
# Purpose: pulls the published images on this machine while they are private, for installing or testing from the
#   registry instead of building from source. Sign Docker in with
#   `printf %s "$GHCR_TOKEN" | docker login ghcr.io -u <your GitHub username> --password-stdin`.
# Where to get it: GitHub › Settings › Developer settings › Personal access tokens (classic), scope `read:packages`
#   only, with an expiry.
GHCR_TOKEN=
